==English==
===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[run]] [[out]]}}
#{{cricket}} The method of getting out in which a [[batsman]], in making a run, has not reached the [[popping crease]] when a [[fielder]] breaks his [[wicket]] with the [[ball]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=to [[run]] [[out]]|runs out|running out|run out}}
#{{idiom}} To [[use up]]; to [[consume]] all of something.
#:''If this hot weather continues, we will '''run out''' of ice cream.''
#{{cricket}} To get a batsman out via a run out (''see above''); ''or'', to be got out in this way.
# A [[contract]] that comes to an end, or an official [[document]] that needs to be [[renewed]], is said to '''run out'''.
#:''My driving licence '''runs out''' next week, so I had better renew it now.''
# To [[extend]] a piece of material, or clothing.
#:''If I '''run out''' these curtains, they will fit the windows in the drawing room.''

